 the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Future Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you use the Future tense in the negative form, you can use the auxiliary <span class=\"italic\">will</span>. </br><span class=\"italic\">Structure: will </span><span class=\"italic strong\">not</span> + base form of the verb </br><span class=\"italic\">Short Form:  </span><span class=\"strong italic\">won't</span> + base form of the verb", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use this form to: </br><ul><li>describe a simple action in the future </br> <span class=\"italic\">They won't help us prepare the meals.</span> </br><il><li> make a prediction </br> <span class=\"italic\">The manager won't give you a raise with that behavior. </span><il></ul> <br/> <br/>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Quantifiers ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use quantifiers to talk about the quantity or amount of something. They can be used with countable and uncountable nouns. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Quantifiers\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">all </br>enough </br>no/none</br> not any </br>some </br>any </br>a lot of </br>lots of </br>plenty of</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">We have to peel all the tomatoes.</span>", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">We prepare all the the menus.  </span>", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">There are plenty of chances to work with them.  </span>", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You have lots of information to review. </span>", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "training session", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a period dedicated to a specific activity", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have a training session with the kitchen manager. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about jobs in restaurants. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to oversee ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be in charge of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You will oversee the food production. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "day-to-day", "type": "name"}, {"content": "happening every day", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You are in charge of day-to-day tasks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "operations", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the work or activities done by a business or organization", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Here is a list of the restaurant's operations. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "food preparation", "type": "name"}, {"content": "preparing food for eating", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You will be directing all food preparation. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "kitchen helper", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone who keeps the kitchen at a restaurant clean and in order", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You'll support the training of kitchen helpers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to require", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to need something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You won't be required to keep track of them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to monitor", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to watch and notice changes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You don't have to monitor the supplies.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob05aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "inventory", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a list of all the things in a place", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You are not looking over the inventory.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob05aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "menu planner", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who organizes meals in advance", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can work with the menu planners to create new dishes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob05aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Choose a job you would like to have.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 6-7 sentences about the actions you have to do in this job. Remember to use the Simple Future tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 1 sentence about an event that happens in this job.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your sentences aloud to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen to their sentences.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about jobs and work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use the Simple Future tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my sentences aloud.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I listen to my partner's sentences. ", "type": "text"}]}]}